statement:
Let n, N, m ∈ ℕ, M, U, N₀ ⊆ ℝᴺ, S_i ⊆ ℝᴺ (i ∈ ℕ) and f : ℝᴺ → ℝᵐ. Assume:
- U is open and M ⊆ U.
- f is locally Lipschitz on U (Mathlib LocallyLipschitzOn: every x ∈ U has K ∈ ℝ≥0 and a neighbourhood t of x within U on which f is K-Lipschitz).
- Every S_i satisfies the frozen IsC1Submanifold n: every y ∈ S_i has an open V ⊆ ℝⁿ, an open W ⊆ ℝᴺ with y ∈ W, and ψ : ℝⁿ → ℝᴺ such that ψ is C¹ on V, injective on V, ψ(V) = W ∩ S_i, satisfies the properness clause, and Dψ(x) is injective for every x ∈ V.
- M ⊆ N₀ ∪ ⋃_i S_i.
Then there are sets D_α ⊆ ℝⁿ and maps ψ_α : ℝⁿ → ℝᴺ (α ∈ ℕ) such that, for every α:
- D_α is open;
- ψ_α is C¹ on D_α (ContDiffOn ℝ 1) and injective on D_α;
- ψ_α is Lipschitz on D_α with some constant K ∈ ℝ≥0;
- Dψ_α(u) = fderiv ℝ ψ_α u is injective for every u ∈ D_α;
- f ∘ ψ_α is Lipschitz on D_α with some constant;
and M ⊆ N₀ ∪ ⋃_α ψ_α(D_α). Notation: ℝᵈ = Rn d = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d).
